{
  "name": "gkz_series_removable_zero",
  "kind": "gkz_series",
  "note": "Issue #88: beta=(-1,0,0), weight (1,1,1,0); ker A is spanned by l=(1,1,1,-3) and the indicial polynomial along theta=(t,t,t-1,-3t) is t^2(t-1). The exponent (0,0,-1,0) has multiplicity 2; its perturbed coefficient at u=l, (-3e)(-3e-1)(-3e-2)/(e(1+e)^2) = -6-15e+..., has a removable zero, and the second solution is x3^-1 (log z + z(-15-6 log z)) with z=x^l. Its part at x^(1,1,0,-3), the other exponent, has a logarithm, so it is not canonical (Issue #75)",
  "category": "resonant",
